daemon: Latch click-and-drag across firmware button dropouts

The Sensel firmware's pressure bit (the touchpad button) drops out while a
finger slides during a click and drag, because the pressure falls, and does not
come back. The button released in the middle of the drag.

Once a confirmed press is followed by exactly one contact moving
[Touchpad] DragStartMm (default 1.5), a drag is latched and releases of the
firmware bit are ignored. The latch ends when the dragging contact lifts (the
contacts already have LiftGraceMs applied), when all contacts are gone, or when
the bit is released and the contacts stay still (less than 0.5 mm) for
[Touchpad] DragReleaseStillMs (default 300; 0 releases only on lift). A
re-press of the bit during the latch continues the drag. A palm block or
disabling the device ends it. Clicks without movement still release at once.

The runner timeout from LiftGraceMs is reused so the stillness release also
happens if the sensor stops sending frames. While latched, the singletouch lift
no longer clears BTN_LEFT behind the latch's back.

The two-finger scroll cancel of ButtonMaxMoveMm now counts the contacts that
moved instead of looking at the farthest one: a drag with a second, resting
contact (thumb) is no longer cancelled; two moving contacts still are.

