 ##
 # LiftGraceMs = 30
 
+##
+## Drag latch. Once a button press is confirmed and exactly one contact then moves this far
+## (in millimeters), a drag has begun and releases of the firmware's button bit are ignored,
+## because the bit drops out while the finger slides (pressure falls). The button is then
+## released when the dragging contact lifts (after LiftGraceMs), or when the bit is released
+## and the contacts stay still (less than 0.5 mm) for DragReleaseStillMs. A re-press of the
+## bit during the latch continues the drag. Clicks without movement release immediately.
+## DragStartMm = 0 disables the latch. (Default 1.5)
+##
+# DragStartMm = 1.5
+
+##
+## How long (in milliseconds) the button bit must stay released and the contacts must stay
+## still before a latched drag is released. 0 releases only when the contact lifts.
+## (Default 300)
+##
+# DragReleaseStillMs = 300
+
 [Contacts]
 ##
 ## How the neutral value of the heatmap will be determined.
